[{:db/id "q-328066/field-1/4af8d3bd922f8f9b189131f5df87225d6fb81cbf4ab0ebfa784a0c499b2eb63c" :answer/id #uuid "4bc84880-6e9a-5753-b9ca-312573979730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-d-a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328066/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9cda418-315a-51b2-83f5-c2dddd2b4c42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328066/field-1/4af8d3bd922f8f9b189131f5df87225d6fb81cbf4ab0ebfa784a0c499b2eb63c" :answer-field/choices ["q-328066/field-1/4af8d3bd922f8f9b189131f5df87225d6fb81cbf4ab0ebfa784a0c499b2eb63c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328066" :question/id #uuid "ceacc4af-4ece-5930-b5ef-87e857f1b68c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328066" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0eccac1629f5ab7d80fe4a7a6d4b1f58867adeed023e957f1f52daa885a745fa.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=$ \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/c3abc51a0c48faa7853eb2ef605412ca6311866994b15a579b7bc7e7db63ee15.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=-d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/a53de4a8dcbd4a5d1f7640d5e1d4c8b6fd6e5e24388f432d279392727b11dd59.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =-d+(-a) \\\\  & =-d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-328066/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328086/field-1/341fea58d539c3ea67debad889d05fd13f91cc01225a4aabc34e5c25512d2af4" :answer/id #uuid "dea8b1e2-5c3b-5aaa-b2f0-a3528c417c58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-b-c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328086/field-1/bbfee62f645deb84983b5a1dab15c0b9544ec4e11ce85ed254db32eb461a1da8" :answer/id #uuid "3db78896-d0f1-5cce-a610-5fc6317807b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b+c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328086/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e351ee66-0add-5f2c-8052-3aeed686e669" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328086/field-1/341fea58d539c3ea67debad889d05fd13f91cc01225a4aabc34e5c25512d2af4" :answer-field/choices ["q-328086/field-1/341fea58d539c3ea67debad889d05fd13f91cc01225a4aabc34e5c25512d2af4" "q-328086/field-1/bbfee62f645deb84983b5a1dab15c0b9544ec4e11ce85ed254db32eb461a1da8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328086" :question/id #uuid "c081346a-0e68-599c-87e2-af148437aebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-328086" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-328086/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328086"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327824/field-1/795fd2398663ce58714d79930a2233be6bf5f6d76d3255eae112a58688cc2f97" :answer/id #uuid "95a3eb68-2bfa-5f72-862a-64a4c903b7fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "d+a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327824/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ade2e86c-86a0-5c20-8f8d-2be6dd14299e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327824/field-1/795fd2398663ce58714d79930a2233be6bf5f6d76d3255eae112a58688cc2f97" :answer-field/choices ["q-327824/field-1/795fd2398663ce58714d79930a2233be6bf5f6d76d3255eae112a58688cc2f97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327824" :question/id #uuid "04b07630-88ca-5b82-aa19-f75f0ac3af5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-327824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4290dec2be26edf6d3b12bf6ffb0fd69cfe9f672dbd02fd970c1bfc3e8c01c2a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=d,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RP}$ in terms of vectors $a,d,$ and $c.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $d,$ and $c.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RP}=$  \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,d,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/b6eb4bdf68dcecd124ec7129b94b6c5adccc826f505ecda653069640efa439e2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/90749b45c5e992ba17f09c6a3597adebcdad2ab9d354b2aee7e41058af69863a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RP} & =\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327824/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275812/field-1/8020078787079441cb8b58e6d2feab3ce8bb788967a8edbad7a8c9795db56138" :answer/id #uuid "7feac72a-dd34-551e-a964-09cd98b5c876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b-c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275812/field-1/bbfee62f645deb84983b5a1dab15c0b9544ec4e11ce85ed254db32eb461a1da8" :answer/id #uuid "54c1f316-d090-5d41-af68-e818b4d92a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b+c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275812/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c60d797b-4b35-50ae-aa74-6e4c5b693a50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275812/field-1/8020078787079441cb8b58e6d2feab3ce8bb788967a8edbad7a8c9795db56138" :answer-field/choices ["q-275812/field-1/8020078787079441cb8b58e6d2feab3ce8bb788967a8edbad7a8c9795db56138" "q-275812/field-1/bbfee62f645deb84983b5a1dab15c0b9544ec4e11ce85ed254db32eb461a1da8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275812" :question/id #uuid "536d1bf1-889a-5747-85c9-b48e01a5c1f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275812" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/3db9a8b3774e6d05efa1d3cbe262a16e2824f249c9fecfebf605ec8de7ca0634.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{AB}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{EB}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{EC}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DC}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{CB}$ in terms of vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{CB}=$    \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $C$ to $B$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/1c1826cfb7602c6380fed1e2aa3c380f575a29185c46ca969d212d94f7c11aed.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CE}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EB}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/c013029af2f1d0dd727ac3c2dc701334fe51a9391b9691144a12f4cfff25c3d5.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =-c+b \\\\  & =b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275812/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection/c5441fb5e93380e3dba68a6ddc1311f38cf3948452c9364c2b743827718bcfa8" :answer/id #uuid "b95204dc-33a0-537b-8fad-dbc7ec4a03d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{TS}=a-b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection/68f9b515f6650c2ebbeb795e7a1b6391034e31de4254c495af8a86ba029827d5" :answer/id #uuid "c0643964-42aa-566c-84a8-649e80912570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{TS}=d-c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection/d591a4f239150fa57808847ba170d8707970c49f95cafea103c92d3cb32f6731" :answer/id #uuid "a6b4e738-2b0a-5fab-8a62-1704f44389e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{TS}=d+b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection/62722e082a27b0c25cf69c91b423aab3220c3db293eea2ddc703b1aecfbc0304" :answer/id #uuid "d99872b3-db7a-5ab1-b76e-b5a65f749c7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{TS}=a-c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection/66b7c34e13cfbe7749a60d3ffb3904b63af1330e9db5c631789de53ecdd94a7d" :answer/id #uuid "675d5d27-dedc-5e78-8b8b-9a4ee4be783d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{TS}=a+c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69531/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "242bf1ca-62ed-542e-b8e0-b82f7b6c2d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-f